    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101821" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχεδ-όθεν</span></b> , Adv., prop. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from nigh at hand</i>; but used
			much like sq., <i>nigh at hand, near</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤμων μεσσηγὺς ς. βάλε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.807
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.662
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. δέ οἱ ἦλθεν Ἀθήνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.267
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				13.221
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῆ ῥ᾽ αὐτῶν ς</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				19.447
			</span></i>.</div>
